# 52
#title Add build:win:installer for the Squirrel installer
#url https://github.com/MobileReality/lantern/pull/52
#branch feat/windows-installer-build
#base feat/windows-installer
#opened 2026-11-13
#head a8d772da69dfb49b21ce3f025be393283d4a67a8
#describe what A build:win:installer command builds a Squirrel.Windows installer from the packaged Windows app, leaving the setup file, the update index and a full package, and failing when one is missing.
#describe before Only the portable Windows zip could be built.
#describe after The installer, RELEASES and lantern-<version>-full.nupkg are also built into dist.
#describe verified Typecheck and tests pass; the real Squirrel build cannot run on macOS and is checked by CI once the release workflow wires it.
#plan windows-squirrel-installer s3.1
+ scripts/build-windows-installer.mjs
+ test/build-windows-installer.test.ts
~ package.json
~ pnpm-lock.yaml
#order scripts/build-windows-installer.mjs
#order package.json
#order pnpm-lock.yaml
#order test/build-windows-installer.test.ts
#reason scripts/build-windows-installer.mjs The release needs an installer from the packaged app, with pure option and output checks that can fail without Windows
#reason test/build-windows-installer.test.ts Proves the options and the three-output check without a Windows build
#reason package.json Adds the build:win:installer command and lets pnpm run the installer tool's install script that selects 7z.exe
#reason pnpm-lock.yaml Lockfile, asset or generated file; nothing to reason about beyond its source.
#story Building the Windows installer
#step actor A maintainer on Windows
#file package.json
#step action runs the installer command after packaging
#step subject the packaged Windows app
#file scripts/build-windows-installer.mjs
#below interaction Get a setup file, an update index and a full package
#below consequence Only a portable zip could be shipped => A real installer is built, and a missing output fails the build
#file test/build-windows-installer.test.ts
